Source: lincmox
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Florent GAUDIN <florent.gaudin@lincmox.ovh>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), golang-go (>= 1.22)
Standards-Version: 4.6.0
Homepage: https://doc.lincmox.ovh

Package: lincmox
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: LincMox CLI — LincStation LED control for Proxmox VE
 Command-line interface to control LincStation N1 LEDs via I2C.
 When lincmoxd is running, commands are transparently routed through
 its Unix socket instead of accessing the I2C bus directly.

Package: lincmoxd
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, lincmox
Description: LincMox daemon — REST API and Web UI for LincStation LED control
 Background daemon that exposes a REST API and an embedded Web UI
 to control LincStation N1 LEDs. Includes background monitors that
 can automatically drive LEDs based on system metrics (network
 activity, disk I/O, etc.).

